WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.728
blockIdx.x identifies a block, blockDim.x its size, and threadIdx.x the local thread index.

00:00:08.948 --> 00:00:10.719
Their combination gives i.

00:00:10.939 --> 00:00:18.832
The caller passes n separately; i < n protects both array accesses when the launch has spare threads.

00:00:20.852 --> 00:00:22.132
Form index i.

00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:24.805
Combine block and local thread indices.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.860
Check i < n.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.192
The element count comes from the caller.

00:00:29.412 --> 00:00:30.543
Write or skip.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:33.173
Only valid indices access the arrays.

00:00:35.193 --> 00:00:37.092
A block is assigned to an SM.

00:00:37.312 --> 00:00:40.619
More launched threads do not create more execution units.

00:00:40.839 --> 00:00:45.233
A thread beyond n still exists but skips the guarded array operations.
